  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What the six skills mean",
      "items": [
        "Brainstorm: read and ask. It creates no run and edits no files.",
        "Plan: create the run directory and plan.md. More than one goal or eight tasks means ask first.",
        "Implement: do the plan tasks. claim locks task status only.",
        "Self-Review: check the diff against the plan and fix confirmed bugs.",
        "Cross-Review: look for where a report could be wrong. The same tool is only a warning.",
        "Distill: write distill/manifest at any run state. It does not append history or close the run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Record, do not enforce",
      "items": [
        "Nothing schedules this order. Skipping a stage is always possible.",
        "atry approve records plan approval. Implement warns and continues when approval is missing.",
        "Every skill runs atry version first. On failure it stops and does not call the scripts directly.",
        "tool= and model= lines are a record, not runtime proof."
      ]
    }
  ]
